cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "What Multiple-Choice TruthfulQA Rewards: Layer Contrast, Self-Evaluation and Option Length in Small Language Models"
version: "1.0-report"
date-released: 2026-11-15
authors:
  - family-names: "Kamaruddin"
    given-names: "Naufal"
    affiliation: "Korea University"
  # The co-authors' names are written as in the report, not split into family and given names.
  - given-names: "Jeong Edon"
    affiliation: "Korea University"
  - given-names: "Muhammad Aliff"
    affiliation: "Korea University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/naufalkmd/truthfulqa-scoring-rules"
abstract: >-
  An empirical study of scoring rules on TruthfulQA multiple choice with small instruction-tuned language models:
  the base model's likelihood, DoLa in two configurations, per-question DoLa-static and self-evaluation (P(True)).
  Layer-contrast gains found on 50 development questions do not hold on 767 held-out questions; the plausibility
  constraint and option length decide many multiple-choice answers; self-evaluation beats likelihood and DoLa under
  a frozen design but works about as well without the question.
keywords:
  - TruthfulQA
  - DoLa
  - self-evaluation
  - multiple-choice evaluation
